# NOTE: tests/cassettes/*.yaml is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# Cassettes are the point of #105: recorded upstream bytes, committed so the
# suite runs against what a service actually sent rather than a fixture
# someone wrote. An ignore rule here silently defeats the whole feature --
# run 33414811346 recorded all three feeds, scanned them for credentials,
# played them back, and then committed nothing, every step green.
#
# Credentials are handled by scrubbing (tests/vcr_config.py) and by the
# recorder's structural + literal scanner, which CI asserts. Not by hiding
# the files from git.
